  "id": "anticipatory-nausea",
  "term": "anticipatory nausea",
  "definition": "Anticipatory nausea is nausea that occurs before chemotherapy, typically when a patient is re-exposed to the treatment setting or related clinical cues. In psychology, it is commonly understood as a learned response and a classic example used in discussions of Pavlovian conditioning.",
